Can you share an example of a leader who inspired you to not only reach your potential, but also exceed it, and explain how they did so using a C# code example?
For instance, my previous manager motivated me to improve my coding skills by providing me with challenging tasks and offering constructive feedback. Here's a C# code snippet that demonstrates the type of project he assigned to me:
```csharp
public class CustomList<T>
{
    private T[] items;
    private int count;
    public CustomList()
    {
        items = new T[4];
        count = 0;
    }
    public void Add(T item)
    {
        if (count == items.Length)
        {
            ResizeArray();
        }
        items[count] = item;
        count++;
    }
    private void ResizeArray()
    {
        T[] tempArray = new T[items.Length * 2];
        for (int i = 0; i < items.Length; i++)
        {
            tempArray[i] = items[i];
        }
        items = tempArray;
    }
}
```
My manager tasked me with implementing a custom list in C# that could add items dynamically and automatically resize the underlying array when necessary. Through this project, I was able to improve my understanding of data structures and algorithms and ultimately exceeded my own expectations.

